hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24270","Abu Sa'id, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Matar ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, I heard Hind bint al-Wazza' that she heard al-Wazza' say: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with al-Ashajj al-Mundhir ibn Amir, or Amir ibn al-Mundhir, and with them was a stricken man. So they came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and when they saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), they leapt from their mounts and came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and kissed his hand. Then al-Ashajj alighted, tied his mount, took out his bag and opened it, and brought out two white garments of his clothes and wore them. Then he came to their mounts and tied them, then came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O Ashajj, in you are two traits which Allah and His Messenger love: forbearance and deliberation. So he said: O Messenger of Allah, have I acquired them, or has Allah fashioned me upon them? He said: Rather, Allah has fashioned you upon them. He said: Praise be to Allah who fashioned me upon two traits which Allah and His Messenger love. So al-Wazza' said: O Messenger of Allah, with me is a maternal uncle of mine who is stricken, so supplicate to Allah for him. So he said: Where is he? Bring him to me. He said: So I did as al-Ashajj did; I dressed him in his two garments and brought him. So he took his cloak and raised it until we saw the whiteness of his armpit, then struck his back and said: Come out, enemy of Allah. So he turned his face, looking with the gaze of a healthy man."
